  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Lovesac is navigating a persistently soft furniture cycle but continues to capture modest market share, underscoring relative resilience. The company is building toward its most prolific year of new product introductions, betting on innovation to differentiate itself from peers and stimulate demand. While end-market weakness keeps the top-line story muted, the qualitative narrative is shifting away from a consumer recovery play and toward a self-help margin improvement story driven by mix and operational levers.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing a disciplined margin expansion agenda, emphasizing structural cost control and a planned move to U.S. manufacturing to lock in higher gross margins. The team’s ability to deliver a smaller-than-feared loss and raise near-term margin guidance has bolstered credibility. With a net-cash, debt-free balance sheet providing ample runway, management is leaning into aggressive product investment while maintaining tight expense oversight—fueling a narrative that the market may be underappreciating a coming profit inflection as industry headwinds eventually abate.",
